  "answer": "All five writable files were rewritten; no other files were touched.\n\n**Changes**\n- `normalize.mjs`: now pure/non-mutating. Validates via existing `assertIssue` (throws `TypeError('invalid issue')`), returns a fresh object with property order `id, title, tags, assignee`. ID and title are trimmed with case preserved; tags are trimmed, lowercased, empties dropped, first-occurrence de-duplicated into a new array; assignee trimmed+lowercased with empty → `null`, input `null` stays `null`. Frozen inputs work since nothing is assigned.\n- `consumers/list.mjs`: no longer sorts (removed `localeCompare` sort and in-place `sort` mutation); maps to `normalizeIssue` in input order, fresh array, duplicates kept, `TypeError('issues must be an array')` for non-arrays.\n- `consumers/search.mjs`: validates query string first, builds the normalized list, trims/lowercases the query, returns the whole list for empty query, otherwise filters on normalized title substring or any normalized tag; original order preserved, no ID/assignee matching, fresh array per call.\n- `consumers/activity.mjs`: uses `listIssues` order, renders `id|assignee|tags` with `-` for null assignee and comma-joined tags (empty tags → empty final field).\n- `serialize.mjs`: serializes `listIssues(issues)` so output is normalized, ordered, and free of extra fields.\n\n`legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, `validators.mjs`, fixtures, and the date/paging/console helpers were left unchanged, so `legacyTitle`, `boardSnapshot` key order, and unrelated exports keep their behavior.\n\n**Verification**: no execution environment was available, so nothing was run — including `public.test.mjs`. Correctness was checked by reading the code against the stated contract only.",
